\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Awake, glad soul, awake, awake!
\par Thy Lord hath risen long;
\par Go to His grave, and with thee take
\par Both tuneful heart and song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where life is walking all around,
\par Where love's sweet voices sing,
\par The first bright blossoms may be found,
\par Of an eternal spring.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The shade and gloom of life are fled
\par This resurrection day;
\par Henceforth in Christ are no more dead,
\par The grave hath no more prey.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In Christ we live, in Christ we sleep,
\par In Christ we wake and rise;
\par And the sad tears death makes us weep,
\par He wipes from all our eyes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then wake, glad heart, awake, awake!
\par And seek Thy risen Lord;
\par Joy in His resurrection take,
\par And comfort in His word.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And let thy life through all its ways
\par One long thanksgiving be;
\par Its theme of joy, its song of praise-
\par Christ died and rose for me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

